      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "**The Bit**: On stage, John Wilson, notorious radio shock-jock, leans confidently in front of a sea of bewildered faces at a high-profile investment conference. He swigs a soda quietly in the corner, smirking before stepping into the limelight.\n\n(WAITS A MOMENT)\n\nJOHN WILLIAMS:\nLadies and gents, you know, at the $400 million initial coin offering of Helios Innovations, I'd say I had some *spark* more than most. I—you're not listening when you're tuning but it's the frequency that swings the pendulum, right?\n\nEVERYONE IN THE SAHLSI ASHAMES, A BIT AGOG.\n\nJOHN WILLIAMS (CONT'D):\nYou think I just walked in, pulled out my good ol' map, and clicked my heels together like Dorothy—but that’s not all.\n\nI saw this opportunity, and there was a *briefing* with a couple of execs that couldn’t even move when I stopped to say 'hi.' We talk strategy, I kid you not—I warned them about being too direct and not being 'sterayable' enough. See, in my market, any crying wolf or obvious pitch is like playing with",
